## Article

```catala
declaration scope A:
  input d content duration
  internal diff content duration
  output o content integer

scope A:
    definition diff equals |2024-02-16| - |2024-01-16|
    definition o equals -1
    exception definition o
        under condition d<=diff
        consequence equals 0

declaration scope TestA:
    output o content integer

scope TestA:
    definition o equals (output of A with {-- d: 1 month}).o
```

The concolic interpreter finishes without finding any crash...

```catala-test-cli
$ catala Concolic --conc-optim=incremental -s A
┌─[RESULT]─ Concolic execution ─
│ Executed 2 tests:
│           Inputs │ Outputs
│ ──────────── Test #1 ─────
│ d_in = [10 days] │ o = 0
│ ──────────── Test #2 ─────
│ d_in = [32 days] │ o = -1
└─
```

...but the input `[0 years, 1 months, 0 days]`, that cannot be generated by Z3
for now, does crash the scope.
Maybe this warrants a concolic interpreter warning?

```catala-test-cli
$ catala Interpret -s TestA
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  During evaluation: ambiguous comparison between durations in different
│  units (e.g. months vs. days).
│
├─➤ tests/concolic/bad/duration_compare_month.catala_en:13.26-28:
│    │
│ 13 │         under condition d<=diff
│    │                          ‾‾
└─ Article
#return code 123#
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala DCalc -s A
let scope A (A_in: A_in): A =
  let get d : duration = A_in.d_in in
  let set diff : ⟪duration⟫ =
    ⟨ ⟨true ⊢ ⟨|2024-02-16| - |2024-01-16|⟩⟩ | false ⊢ ∅ ⟩
  in
  let set o : integer =
    error_empty
      ⟨ ⟨ ⟨d ≤ error_empty diff ⊢ ⟨0⟩⟩ | false ⊢ ∅ ⟩
      | true ⊢ ⟨ ⟨true ⊢ ⟨-1⟩⟩ | false ⊢ ∅ ⟩ ⟩
  in
  return { A o = o; }
```
